gpu-switcher (0.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Fix: Apply and Reset to auto failed with Error.Internal. The helper called
    invocation.get_cancellable(), a method the real GDBusMethodInvocation does
    not expose in this pygobject build; the resulting AttributeError was caught
    by the dispatcher and surfaced as Error.Internal. A fresh
    Gio.Cancellable is used instead.
  * Fix: the polkit check hung until the client timed out. authorize() passed
    user_data to connection.call, which pygobject forwards to the callback, so
    on_result was invoked with three arguments and raised TypeError before the
    reply completed. The user_data is omitted so the callback keeps its two
    parameters.
  * The helper tests now model the real pygobject invocation and callback
    conventions, catching both mismatches instead of mocking them away.

 -- wl04 <wl04@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 19:32:24 +0100

gpu-switcher (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * New: GPU rows are accessible — the name is now the radio's child, so screen readers announce each card and clicking the label selects it; status banners use Adwaita's success/warning/error styling.
  * Faster detection: the running primary is found by a /proc uid scan (no logind round trip) with journalctl filtering server-side, and GPU names come from the lspci machine format.
  * The helper runs as a D-Bus-activated systemd service, is fully async with a busy lock, reports stable D-Bus error names, and is hardened (python3 -I -B, no site/user .pyc).
  * Fixes: timeouts are matched as G_IO_ERROR_TIMEOUT (7), so real timeouts are reported and the stale polkit dialog is cancelled; the idle-exit timer is armed at startup; SetPrimary survives a non-UTF-8 existing rule; a second app start presents the existing window; a vanished selected card is refused instead of silently switching to auto; actions are disabled outside a GNOME Wayland session.
  * Structure: code split into gpu_switcher.core and gpu_switcher.helper; string states are Enums; bus and selection logic de-duplicated; i18n honours LANGUAGE and derives locales; the hard-coded GPU table is gone (unknown cards show their PCI id).
  * Tooling: CI (test/lint/typecheck, both .deb builds + lintian, systemd-analyze verify), pinned dev tools, a single install list in make install, and mypy now type-checks main.py with disallow_untyped_defs for the core and tests.

 -- wl04 <wl04@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 18:35:08 +0100

gpu-switcher (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fix: the helper no longer crashes (NameError) when its rate-limit cleanup removes expired per-caller entries.
  * The helper's reply messages are now composed from shared building blocks; the wording is unchanged in every shipped language.
  * ruff (lint and format) and mypy (type check) are wired into the local checks (make lint, make typecheck); public contracts are type-annotated.
  * Test suite: snake_case method names, language-agnostic (English primary), and a catalog-completeness guard (no empty or fuzzy translations in any shipped locale).

